m(2,"Cognitive liberation","Douglas McAdam's “cognitive liberation” is a process in which many people collectively decide that…","a grave injustice has occurred, they must act, and they cannot go back",["the regime has lost its legal authority and must be replaced by a tribunal","their personal hardship matters more than the shared cause of the group","the risk of acting is lower than last year and the odds clearly favor them"],"People decide that a grave injustice has taken place, that they must act and get involved, and that they cannot return to the time when they were unaware of it or willing to tolerate it.",2);
