m(3,"Security forces","What did Stephan and Chenoweth find after reviewing more than one hundred campaigns between 1900 and 2006?","Security-force defections greatly raise the odds of success",["Security-force defections rarely change the outcome of campaigns","Nonviolent resistance succeeds only where there are no defections","Defections matter only when the regime is a democracy"],"The nature of the defection varied from generals refusing orders to soldiers putting down their weapons.",2);
